  "narration": {
    "title": "Kansas City Runs the Table, Storms the Board",
    "intro": "Milwaukee is still on top, but the week belonged to the teams behind them. The Royals went 7-0 and leapt nineteen spots, while both the Dodgers and Phillies posted perfect weeks of their own. The top of the power ranking is getting crowded.",
    "power_lead": "The Brewers hold the top spot on a 4-2 week and a season-best plus-161 run differential, with Garrett Mitchell going 8-for-12. The loudest climb is Kansas City, up nineteen into the top ten on a flawless 7-0 run behind Vinnie Pasquantino and a 10-for-27 week from Bobby Witt Jr. Boston jumped twelve to fourth after Mickey Gasper drove in nine over the week, and the Dodgers and Phillies each went 6-0 to sit second and third, Fernando Tatis Jr.'s 4-homer, 11-RBI week keeping San Diego steady at sixth."
  }
